WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:03.634
The question comes first: inventory planning.

2
00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:08.403
Check the grain of the data and its definitions before you draw a chart or build a model.

3
00:00:08.803 --> 00:00:13.572
In Jupyter, check missing periods and separate training data from the validation window.

4
00:00:13.572 --> 00:00:18.992
Inspect seasonality and demand in Excel, then compare a simple baseline with a time-aware forecast.

5
00:00:19.392 --> 00:00:22.134
Show the forecast and its uncertainty in Power BI.

6
00:00:22.134 --> 00:00:24.108
In Tableau, compare product groups.

7
00:00:24.108 --> 00:00:29.701
Use Grafana for the operational signal, keeping the model error visible beside the planning decision.

8
00:00:30.101 --> 00:00:32.249
Publish the story as forecast dashboard.

9
00:00:32.249 --> 00:00:36.651
Let people filter the view, inspect the evidence, and understand the next action.

10
00:00:36.651 --> 00:00:40.463
The presentation should remain clear when the underlying data changes.
